= Sequence alignment — Simple =

Sequence alignment lines up DNA, RNA, or protein sequences so comparable positions can be examined. The alignment is an analytical model; similarity does not by itself prove common ancestry or identical function.

'''Important boundary:''' alignment ≠ proof of homology.

